---

<DocsLayout title="Commands — Tether CLI" description="Every Tether command and its options.">
  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">REFERENCE</p>
    <h1>Commands</h1>
    <p>Run <code>tether &lt;command&gt; --help</code> for the options of each command. Every command takes <code>-y</code>. For <code>-y</code>, exit codes, <code>--json</code>, machine arguments and package ids, see <a href="/docs/scripting">Exit codes and -y</a>.</p>

    <h3 id="cmd-dashboard">tether / tether dashboard</h3>
    <p>Open the interactive dashboard. See <a href="/docs/dashboard">Dashboard</a>.</p>
    <Code code="tether" />

    <h3 id="cmd-init">tether init</h3>
    <p>Set up Tether on this machine. It asks for the repository and the passphrase, runs the first sync, and installs the daemon. See <a href="/docs/quick-start">Quick start</a>.</p>
    <Code code="tether init [--repo <URL>] [--no-daemon] [--team-only]" />
    <ul>
      <li><code>--repo &lt;URL&gt;</code>: the Git repository URL. Without it, Tether asks</li>
      <li><code>--no-daemon</code>: do not install the daemon</li>
      <li><code>--team-only</code>: skip personal dotfiles and packages, and use team sync only</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="cmd-sync">tether sync</h3>
    <p>Sync now. See <a href="/docs/how-it-works">How sync works</a>.</p>
    <Code code="tether sync [--dry-run] [--rediscover]" />
    <ul>
      <li><code>--dry-run</code>: show what a sync would do. It ends with "Dry run: nothing changed"</li>
      <li><code>--rediscover</code>: ask again about file imports that you dismissed</li>
    </ul>
    <p>In a terminal, <code>tether sync</code> asks about conflicts and about items in the Inbox. Without a terminal, it runs as the daemon does: it records conflicts for <code>tether resolve</code> and holds Inbox items. On macOS, a sync in a terminal also moves an installed daemon to <code>~/.tether/bin/tether</code>.</p>

    <h3 id="cmd-status">tether status</h3>
    <p>Show the sync status, the daemon state, this machine's profile and the synced files. It counts the items in the Inbox and the files with conflicts. It names each machine that still runs 1.x.</p>
    <Code code="tether status [--json]" />

    <h3 id="cmd-diff">tether diff</h3>
    <p>Show differences between machines.</p>
    <Code code="tether diff [--machine <MACHINE>]" />

    <h3 id="cmd-daemon">tether daemon</h3>
    <p>Control the background daemon.</p>
    <Code code={`tether daemon start
tether daemon stop
tether daemon restart
tether daemon status
tether daemon logs [-f] [-n <LINES>]
tether daemon install
tether daemon uninstall`} />
    <ul>
      <li><code>status</code>: whether the daemon runs, whether its login service is installed, and the last sync and upgrade</li>
      <li><code>logs</code>: print the end of the daemon log. <code>-n</code> sets the number of lines (default 50). <code>-f</code> keeps printing lines as the daemon writes them</li>
      <li><code>install</code>: install the login service. On macOS, a launchd agent runs a copy of Tether at <code>~/.tether/bin/tether</code> and follows upgrades by itself. On Linux, a systemd user service. See <a href="/docs/linux">Linux and systemd</a></li>
      <li><code>uninstall</code>: remove the login service. On macOS, it also removes the copy</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="cmd-machines">tether machines</h3>
    <p>List, show, trust and remove machines, and manage profiles. See <a href="/docs/trust">Machine trust</a>.</p>
    <Code code={`tether machines list [--json]
tether machines show [MACHINE]
tether machines rename <NEW>
tether machines remove <MACHINE>
tether machines trust <MACHINE> [--fingerprint SHA256:...]
tether machines untrust <MACHINE>
tether machines profile <set|unset|create|edit|list>`} />
    <ul>
      <li><code>list</code>: every machine with its profile, version, last sync, key fingerprint and trust. It marks machines on 1.x, and records that may be an old id of this machine</li>
      <li><code>show [MACHINE]</code>: one machine's profile, versions, record status, full key fingerprint and trust. Without a machine, it shows this machine</li>
      <li><code>rename &lt;NEW&gt;</code>: rename this machine. Tether signs its record again under the new id. Other machines must trust the new id. The form <code>rename &lt;OLD&gt; &lt;NEW&gt;</code> still works in 2.0 with a warning, and fails when OLD is not this machine</li>
      <li><code>remove &lt;MACHINE&gt;</code>: remove a machine record, and its trusted key on this machine. With <code>-y</code>, Tether removes it without a question and prints what it removed</li>
      <li><code>trust &lt;MACHINE&gt; --fingerprint SHA256:...</code>: trust a machine's signing key if its fingerprint matches. Without a fingerprint, Tether shows the current one and asks, in a terminal only. When the signed record is missing, it pulls the sync repo first</li>
      <li><code>untrust &lt;MACHINE&gt;</code>: stop trusting a machine's signing key</li>
      <li><code>profile set &lt;PROFILE&gt;</code>: assign a profile to this machine. Each machine sets only its own profile</li>
      <li><code>profile unset</code>: remove the profile assignment of this machine</li>
      <li><code>profile create &lt;PROFILE&gt; [--from &lt;PROFILE&gt;] [--managers &lt;LIST&gt;]</code>: create a profile. See <a href="/docs/profiles">Profiles</a></li>
      <li><code>profile edit &lt;PROFILE&gt;</code>: edit a profile</li>
      <li><code>profile list</code>: list all profiles and assignments</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="cmd-packages">tether packages</h3>
    <p>List, install, share and uninstall packages, and decide on the Inbox.</p>
    <Code code={`tether packages [list] [--json] [--other-profiles]
tether packages install <ID>
tether packages share <ID> --to <PROFILES>
tether packages unshare <ID> --from <PROFILES>
tether packages uninstall [ID]                    # alias: remove
tether packages inbox [--json]
tether packages approve <ID> [--expect <VERSION|TAP|KEY>] [--allow-signature-failed]
tether packages approve --all [--from <MACHINE>]
tether packages reject <ID> [--expect <VERSION|TAP|KEY>]`} />
    <ul>
      <li><code>list</code>: installed packages by manager, with the profiles of each and this machine's profile. It also shows failed installs. A bare <code>tether packages</code> lists too</li>
      <li><code>list --other-profiles</code>: instead, the packages of other profiles that trusted machines list and this machine does not install</li>
      <li><code>install &lt;ID&gt;</code>: install a package that another machine lists, as the dashboard's Import does. OSV checks the release first. A package that waits in the Inbox needs <code>approve</code> instead</li>
      <li><code>share &lt;ID&gt; --to &lt;PROFILES&gt;</code>: add profiles to the package, so machines in those profiles install it. Separate profiles with commas</li>
      <li><code>unshare &lt;ID&gt; --from &lt;PROFILES&gt;</code>: take profiles off the package. Nothing is uninstalled</li>
      <li><code>uninstall [ID]</code>: uninstall the package here, and take this machine's profile off it. For a package that failed to install, it stops the retries on this machine. Without a package, pick packages in a terminal</li>
      <li><code>inbox</code>: list the packages, taps and machine keys that wait for your approval, grouped by source machine and reason</li>
      <li><code>approve &lt;ID&gt;</code>: install the package, or trust the machine key. <code>machine:&lt;id&gt;</code> works as <code>tether machines trust &lt;id&gt;</code></li>
      <li><code>approve --all [--from &lt;MACHINE&gt;]</code>: approve every package in the Inbox, or every package from one machine. It lists the packages and asks first. Without a terminal, it needs <code>-y</code>. It leaves machine keys, malicious packages, packages whose record fails its signature, and packages without a version or tap to name</li>
      <li><code>--allow-signature-failed</code>: approve a package whose record fails its signature, without a terminal. It needs <code>--expect</code> too. In a terminal, Tether asks instead</li>
      <li><code>reject &lt;ID&gt;</code>: stop offering that version, tap or key</li>
      <li><code>--expect</code>: the version, Homebrew tap or key fingerprint you reviewed, as <code>packages inbox</code> shows it. Required without a terminal. Tether refuses the decision when the item changed</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The 1.x forms still work: <code>packages remove</code>, and <code>approve &lt;ID&gt; &lt;EXPECTED&gt;</code> without <code>--expect</code>.</p>

    <h3 id="cmd-upgrade">tether upgrade</h3>
    <p>Upgrade installed packages to the newest release that the release-age limit allows.</p>
    <Code code="tether upgrade [--dry-run]" />
    <ul>
      <li>Tether lists what it will change and asks first. Without a terminal, it needs <code>-y</code></li>
      <li><code>--dry-run</code> lists what an upgrade would change, and which packages stay because the release-age limit allows only an older version</li>
      <li>An upgrade never downgrades a package. It installs only a target newer than the installed version, at that exact version</li>
      <li>Tether checks each npm, pnpm, bun, uv and gem target against OSV. A target with a <code>MAL-</code> advisory waits in the Inbox, and the installed version stays</li>
      <li>Tether asks before it upgrades a manager that cannot enforce the release-age limit. Without a terminal, or with <code>-y</code>, it skips that manager</li>
      <li>Homebrew upgrades include only outdated packages from trusted taps. Tether does not run <code>brew update</code></li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="cmd-rollback">tether rollback</h3>
    <p>Roll back a package manager's installed packages to a manifest commit. The managers are npm, pnpm, bun, gem and uv. Homebrew is not supported.</p>
    <Code code="tether rollback packages <MANAGER> <COMMIT>" />
    <p>Tether lists each package and version it would install, and asks first. Without a terminal, it needs <code>-y</code>. A snapshot version other than the newest trusted version installs only when you confirm it in a terminal. <code>-y</code> does not confirm it. Packages that fail a check wait in the Inbox.</p>

    <h3 id="cmd-config">tether config</h3>
    <p>Manage configuration. See <a href="/docs/configuration">Configuration</a>.</p>
    <Code code={`tether config get <KEY>
tether config set <KEY> <VALUE>
tether config edit
tether config dotfiles
tether config features [enable|disable <FEATURE>]`} />
    <ul>
      <li><code>get</code>: read a value. Use nested keys such as <code>packages.brew.enabled</code></li>
      <li><code>set</code>: set a value. Tether reads the value as TOML, so arrays work: <code>'["azure/kubelogin"]'</code>. A bare word stays a string. Tether refuses a key that the config does not have</li>
      <li><code>edit</code>: open the config in your editor. It needs a terminal</li>
      <li><code>dotfiles</code>: pick the files, folders and patterns that sync</li>
      <li><code>features</code>: list, enable or disable <a href="/docs/configuration#feature-toggles">feature toggles</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="cmd-ignore">tether ignore</h3>
    <p>Manage secret scanning patterns, and files this machine keeps.</p>
    <Code code={`# Patterns the secret scanner skips
tether ignore secrets add <PATTERN>
tether ignore secrets list
tether ignore secrets remove <PATTERN>

# Files this machine keeps: a sync does not overwrite them
tether ignore files add <FILE>
tether ignore files project <PROJECT> <PATH>
tether ignore files list
tether ignore files remove <FILE>      # sync the file again`} />
    <p>The 1.x forms <code>ignore add|list|remove</code> and <code>ignore dotfile|project|sync-list|sync-remove</code> still work.</p>

    <h3 id="cmd-resolve">tether resolve</h3>
    <p>Resolve file conflicts: keep local, use remote, launch the merge tool, or skip. Without a file, it resolves all. See <a href="/docs/conflicts">Conflicts</a>.</p>
    <Code code="tether resolve [FILE]" />

    <h3 id="cmd-unlock"><span id="cmd-lock"></span>tether unlock / tether lock</h3>
    <p><code>unlock</code> decrypts the encryption key with your passphrase and caches it. <code>lock</code> clears the cached key. See <a href="/docs/encryption">Encryption</a>.</p>
    <Code code={`tether unlock
tether lock`} />

    <h3 id="cmd-history">tether history</h3>
    <p>Show the change history of a dotfile from the sync repo.</p>
    <Code code="tether history <FILE> [--limit <N>]   # default 20" />

    <h3 id="cmd-restore">tether restore</h3>
    <p>Restore files from a backup or from git history.</p>
    <Code code={`tether restore list                          # list backups
tether restore file                          # pick a file and a backup
tether restore file <FILE> --from <TIMESTAMP>
tether restore git <FILE> [--commit <SHA>]   # a dotfile from git history`} />

    <h3 id="cmd-identity">tether identity</h3>
    <p>Manage the age identity for team secrets.</p>
    <Code code={`tether identity init     # make a new identity
tether identity show     # show your public key
tether identity unlock   # unlock with your passphrase
tether identity lock     # clear the cached key
tether identity reset    # make a new identity; destroys the old one`} />

    <h3 id="cmd-team">tether team</h3>
    <p>Manage team repositories, secrets, files and project secrets. See <a href="/docs/team-sync">Teams and collab</a>.</p>
    <Code code={`tether team setup
tether team add <URL> [--name <NAME>]
tether team list
tether team switch <NAME>
tether team status
tether team enable | disable
tether team remove [NAME]

tether team orgs add | list | remove <ORG>

tether team secrets add-recipient <KEY> [--name <NAME>]
tether team secrets list-recipients
tether team secrets remove-recipient <NAME>
tether team secrets set <NAME> [--value <VALUE>]
tether team secrets get <NAME>
tether team secrets list
tether team secrets remove <NAME>

tether team files list
tether team files local-patterns
tether team files diff [FILE]
tether team files reset [FILE] [--all]
tether team files promote <FILE>
tether team files ignore <FILE>
tether team files unignore <FILE>

tether team projects add <FILE> [--project <PATH>]
tether team projects list
tether team projects remove <FILE> [--project <URL>]
tether team projects migrate
tether team projects purge-personal [--history]`} />

    <h3 id="cmd-collab">tether collab</h3>
    <p>Share project secrets with GitHub collaborators. Needs the <code>collab_secrets</code> feature. See <a href="/docs/team-sync#collab">Collab secrets</a>.</p>
    <Code code={`tether collab init [--project <PATH>]
tether collab join <URL>
tether collab add <FILE> [--project <PATH>]
tether collab add-project <PATH>
tether collab refresh [--project <PATH>]
tether collab list
tether collab remove [NAME]`} />
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
